+# Modern app build
+
+The build of an app with a backend and a frontend in one repo, the shape ModernAppTemplate
+renders. It runs the app's test suite in a Kubernetes Job, on the tree it checked out, then builds
+the app's images with kaniko and pins them into the app's deploy repo, which Argo CD syncs. Today
+these are DHCPApp, ElectronicsInventory, FieldnotesApp, IoTSupport and ZigbeeControl. Their files
+were first rendered from ModernAppTemplate's template; a file of this type follows the reference
+file below, not the template.
+
+## What is specific to this type
+
+- **The library's step.** [`modernApp.test`](../reference/modernApp.md) carries what every app's
+  test run shares: the Job on the image of `podYaml`'s `modern-app-toolchain` template, the copy of
+  the tree into it, the summary per suite, the JUnit report and the build's description. The file
+  still writes out every stage and calls the step in `Test`, in `script {}`
+  ([LIB-6](../guide/library.md#lib-6)). Its own values are the Job's name, the install and run
+  commands, the services beside the suite, the suite's environment and secrets, and the suites the
+  summary counts ([LIB-3](../guide/library.md#lib-3)).
+- **The `kaniko` template and the `k8s` sidecar**, as in an [image build](image-build.md): the step
+  runs kubectl in the `k8s` container, and so does the pin write ([POD-3](../guide/pod.md#pod-3)).
+- **`Test`, a stage per image, then `Write image pins`**
+  ([GRAN-2](../guide/stage-granularity.md#gran-2), [GRAN-3](../guide/stage-granularity.md#gran-3),
+  [GRAN-4](../guide/stage-granularity.md#gran-4)). The images are built from the tree the suite
+  passed on.
+- **A suite that needs a secret** gets it through the step's `secrets`, with `withVault` around the
+  step's call alone: [SEC-1](../guide/secrets.md#sec-1)'s one exception. Today that is IoTSupport,
+  whose suite needs the Keycloak admin client.
+
+## The reference file
+
+The `ElectronicsInventory/ElectronicsInventory` job's `Jenkinsfile`:
+
+```groovy
+--8<-- "modern-app.groovy"
+```
