+# modernApp
+
+The step the `Test` stage of a [modern app build](../types/modern-app.md) calls. `test` runs the
+app's test suite in a Kubernetes Job, on the tree the file's `Checkout` stage checked out, beside the
+services the suite needs, and reports the result to the build. The step carries what is the same in
+every app's test run: the Job and its toolchain image, the copy of the tree into it, the `run-suite`
+command line, the summary per suite, the JUnit report and the build's description. A value that
+differs per app is an argument with no default.
+
+The step runs kubectl in the `k8s` container, which the pod declares with
+`podYaml(templates: ['k8s'])` ([`podYaml`](podYaml.md)). It is a call on the var's method, so a
+declarative stage runs it in `script {}`. The file still writes out its every stage; the step goes
+inside `Test`.
+
+```groovy
+agent {
+    kubernetes {
+        inheritFrom 'jenkins-agent kaniko'
+        yamlMergeStrategy merge()
+        yaml podYaml(templates: ['k8s'])
+    }
+}
+
+stages {
+    stage('Checkout') {
+        steps {
+            checkout scm
+        }
+    }
+
+    stage('Test') {
+        steps {
+            script {
+                modernApp.test(
+                    job: 'dhcp-app-validation',
+                    install: 'poetry install --no-interaction --without dev',
+                    run: 'poetry run',
+                    suites: ['backend', 'frontend'],
+                    services: [],
+                    env: [:],
+                    secrets: [],
+                )
+            }
+        }
+    }
+}
+```
+
+## Steps
+
+Every argument is required. `services`, `env` and `secrets` may be empty; `job`, `install`, `run`
+and `suites` may not. A missing argument, an empty one where it may not be, or one the step does not
+take fails the build, and the error names it.
+
+### test
+
+`modernApp.test(…)`, in the `k8s` container:
+
+1. tars the workspace, leaving out `.git`, `node_modules`, `.venv`, `.pnpm-store` and
+   `test-results`;
+2. applies a Job named `<job>-<build number>`. Its `validation` container runs the image of
+   `podYaml`'s `modern-app-toolchain` template, as uid 1000, with an emptyDir at `/work`, and the
+   `services` run beside it. The Job's deadline is 60 minutes;
+3. copies the tar into the container, which unpacks it in `/work`, runs `install` there, then
+   `<run> run-suite --output-mode full --junitxml-dir /work/results --retries 2`, and writes
+   run-suite's exit code beside the JUnit files;
+4. once the exit code is written, saves the container's log as `validation.log` and copies the
+   JUnit files into `test-results/`;
+5. writes `validation-summary.log`, a line per suite and a total, archives the logs and the JUnit
+   files, publishes the JUnit report, and sets the build description to
+   `exit=<code>, <n> passed, <n> failed, <n> skipped`;
+6. fails the build when the exit code is missing or not `0`. The error for a missing one names the
+   Job's fail reason, when the Job has one.
+
+The Job is deleted whatever happened, the build's abort included.
+
+| Argument   | What it is                                                                                                                 |
+| ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `job`      | The Job's name, to which the build number is appended, and its `app.kubernetes.io/name` label: `dhcp-app-validation`.      |
+| `install`  | The command that installs the app at the root of the tree: `poetry install --no-interaction --without dev`, `uv sync --locked --no-dev`. |
+| `run`      | The command `run-suite` runs under: `poetry run`, `uv run --no-sync`.                                                      |
+| `suites`   | The suites the summary counts. A suite counts each of run-suite's result lines whose JUnit file stem is its name or starts with `<name>-`. |
+| `services` | The containers beside the suite: maps with `name` and `image`, and any of `env` (name -> value) and `resources` (`requests` and `limits`, each resource name -> quantity). |
+| `env`      | The suite's environment, name -> value. A value is written in the file and is no secret ([SEC-5](../guide/secrets.md#sec-5)). |
+| `secrets`  | Variables of the build's environment that the suite gets under the same name.                                             |
+
+A service reaches the suite on `localhost`. ElectronicsInventory's suite needs an S3 API, which a
+RustFS container gives it:
+
+```groovy
+modernApp.test(
+    job: 'electronics-inventory-validation',
+    install: 'poetry install --no-interaction --without dev',
+    run: 'poetry run',
+    suites: ['backend', 'frontend'],
+    services: [
+        [name: 's3storage', image: 'rustfs/rustfs:latest', env: [
+            RUSTFS_ACCESS_KEY: 's3storage',
+            RUSTFS_SECRET_KEY: 's3storage',
+        ]],
+    ],
+    env: [
+        S3_ENDPOINT_URL: 'http://localhost:9000',
+        S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID: 's3storage',
+        S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY: 's3storage',
+        S3_BUCKET_NAME: 'electronics-inventory-validation',
+    ],
+    secrets: [],
+)
+```
+
+#### secrets
+
+A suite that needs a secret takes it from the build's environment, where `withVault` puts it. The
+file names the variables in `secrets`, and the step adds each to the suite's environment from a
+shell, so the value never enters a Groovy string or a step's arguments
+([SEC-4](../guide/secrets.md#sec-4)). A variable that is not set fails the build, naming it.
+
+`withVault` wraps the step's call and nothing else: [SEC-1](../guide/secrets.md#sec-1)'s one
+exception, for a test that itself needs a secret. IoTSupport's suite needs the Keycloak admin
+client:
+
+```groovy
+withVault([vaultSecrets: [
+    [path: 'kv/jenkins/keycloak-iotsupport-admin', engineVersion: 2, secretValues: [
+        [envVar: 'KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_CLIENT_ID', vaultKey: 'client_id'],
+        [envVar: 'KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_CLIENT_SECRET', vaultKey: 'client_secret'],
+    ]],
+]]) {
+    modernApp.test(
+        // ...
+        secrets: ['KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_CLIENT_ID', 'KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_CLIENT_SECRET'],
+    )
+}
+```
+
+The secret is in the Job's spec while the Job exists, and the step deletes the Job at its end.
+
+## Internals
+
+`testArguments`, `service`, `environment`, `envList`, `jobManifest`, `suiteScript` and `summary`
+check the arguments and work out the Job the step applies and the summary it writes. They are not
+part of what `modernApp` offers a Jenkinsfile.
