-## The toolchain containers run as uid 1000
-
-`iac_toolchain` and `modern_app_toolchain` run as uid 1000, the agent's own user. The checkout and
-whatever the container writes into the workspace then share an owner: git refuses a repository that
-another uid owns.
-
-`iac_toolchain` sets `TF_PLUGIN_CACHE_DIR` to the empty string. The image points it at a KubeCoder
-home overlay that an agent pod lacks, and terraform reports a missing cache directory as a CLI
-configuration error on every run. The empty value leaves the cache off. `modern_app_toolchain`'s
-image points `COREPACK_HOME` and `PNPM_HOME` at such overlays too; uid 1000 owns `/home/ubuntu` in
-the image, so corepack and pnpm create them there, empty on every build.
